load @term/seed/structure/ring
  find ring

# A graded algebra: an algebra split into degree pieces whose products add degrees, so a degree-two times a degree-three
# lands in degree five. The grading is what makes "even part" and "odd part" meaningful, and the even part of a Clifford
# algebra is the spinor-bearing subalgebra. Polynomials are graded by degree, the exterior algebra by oriented extent.
# The form carries the underlying ring; the degree decomposition is the added structure.
form graded-algebra
  link ring, like ring
